WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.097
Now we move from quality to variable meaning.

00:00:03.097 --> 00:00:08.522
Measurement scale tells us which comparisons and arithmetic operations are defensible.

00:00:08.522 --> 00:00:11.977
Nominal and ordinal are categorical scales.

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:15.032
Interval and ratio are numeric scales.

00:00:15.032 --> 00:00:21.057
The key questions are whether order exists, whether differences have a consistent meaning,

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:25.132
and whether zero represents the absence of the measured quantity.

00:00:25.132 --> 00:00:31.202
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:31.202 --> 00:00:36.547
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:43.012
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:43.012 --> 00:00:45.920
floating-point number.
